[h1]Eris Food Expiry (TooltipLib fork)[/h1]

[b]Unofficial fork · Build 42.21 · Singleplayer and multiplayer[/b]

How long before this milk turns? Hover any food: the tooltip shows its freshness and the exact time left before it goes stale and rots. Expand a stack in your inventory to see a thin freshness strip under each item.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/ErisFoodExpiry/main/docs/steam/05-tooltip-fridge.png[/img]

[h2]Two original mods, one fork[/h2]

This mod continues the work of two Workshop items. Thanks to their authors.
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3392259028][B42] eris food expiry[/url]: Build 42 port of eris's food expiry mod, with the Nutritionist option.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3629527156][B42.13] eris food expiry[/url]: update for 42.13 singleplayer, exact times without the trait.
[/list]
Both use the mod ID [i]eris_food_expiry[/i]: this fork is marked incompatible with it. Enable only one of them.

[h2]What you see[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Freshness[/b] bar: full when the food is new, empty when it is rotten.
[*][b]Stale in[/b] and [b]Rotten in[/b]: time left, largest units first (years, months, weeks, days, hours, minutes).
[*]Frozen food: "Frozen: not spoiling". Canned and dry food: "Does not expire".
[*]Option (Options > Mods): require the Nutritionist trait for exact times. A readable package always shows them, like the vanilla nutrition facts. Otherwise you get a rough state: very fresh, fresh, looks okay, starting to rot, almost rotten, rotten.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/ErisFoodExpiry/main/docs/steam/02-fridge.jpg[/img]

[h2]Times that follow the game[/h2]

The time left is computed the way the game ages food:
[list]
[*]sandbox [i]Food Spoilage[/i] speed and [i]Refrigeration Effectiveness[/i];
[*]a fridge or freezer slows spoilage while it has power: a generator, or the grid until the shutoff day, after which the food spoils at normal speed again;
[*]frozen food does not spoil;
[*]each item's own stale and rotten ages (cooked food differs from raw food).
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/ErisFoodExpiry/main/docs/steam/03-frozen.jpg[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/ErisFoodExpiry/main/docs/steam/06-tooltip-frozen.png[/img]

[h2]What changed from the originals[/h2]

[list]
[*]Tooltip lines through [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3694097672]TooltipLib[/url]: no box drawn under the tooltip, no jumping tooltip, works with other tooltip mods.
[*]Fridge without power, frozen food and cooked food give correct times.
[*]Time units always in order: the originals could show "5m 2d 1w" or drop the years.
[*]The "Rotten" state shows again; option texts and translations load in 42.21 (JSON).
[*]The inventory strip no longer overlaps the nutrition or cooking line.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/ErisFoodExpiry/main/docs/steam/04-read-the-label.jpg[/img]

[h2]Multiplayer[/h2]

Display only: nothing is sent to the server and nothing is saved. Install it on the server so clients download it; each player sets the option for themselves. Safe to add to or remove from an existing world.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]

[list]
[*]Build 42.21 or later.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3694097672]TooltipLib[/url].
[/list]

[h2]Languages[/h2]

English, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Polish, Portuguese, Brazilian Portuguese, Russian, Simplified Chinese.

[h2]Support the project[/h2]

Enjoying the mod? A coffee helps fund new features and translations.
